    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first makes a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into windows while keeping the tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field named F. The window operator then acts on that field, so the next representation is still made from carrier features. The equation names X as the window partition output, not as a discarded or pooled summary.",
