      "id": "s03-params",
      "intent": "DQ-CTM-SR uses the second largest parameter count among the five listed methods, so the comparison does not support calling it cheap.",
      "claim": "Table 1 lists CATANet 0.535M, RFDN 0.550M, IMDN 0.715M, DQ-CTM-SR 1.129M, and CARN 1.592M parameters.",
      "narration": "The five methods are ordered by parameter count, from the smallest model to the largest. DQ-CTM-SR sits at one point one two nine million parameters, above three of the five methods. It is the second largest parameter count in this set, even though CARN is larger. The result is competitive with CNN baselines, but the parameter chart does not make DQ-CTM-SR a cheap model.",
